20260527.112908.625 [<kpop..........] [Perfect. The root cause has been confirmed.]
20260527.112908.861 [<kpop..........] [The issue stems from `enn_rust.so` being linked against `libblas.so.3` and `liblapack.so.3`, but lacking CBLAS symbols like]
20260527.112909.179 [<kpop..........] [`cblas_dgemm` and `cblas_ddot` that are missing from `libblas.so.3` in this conda environment. These symbols are available]
20260527.112909.204 [<kpop..........] [in either `libcblas.so.3` or `libopenblas.so.0`. Although the build script `emit_openblas_link` should have used the full]
20260527.112909.379 [<kpop..........] [path to `libopenblas` when `CONDA_PREFIX` was set, the extension incorrectly ended up with `libblas.ne` instead. Runtime]
20260527.112909.741 [<kpop..........] [linking via `LD_PRELOAD` with `libcblas` resolves the issue.]
20260527.112911.448 [<kpop..........] [The build likely occurred when the environment lacked proper linking to the required CBLAS library.]
