20260527.113208.477 [<kpop..........] You likely mean **why you can't** get `pytest tests` to run — I treated it that way (DCC: no code changes).
20260527.113208.522 [<kpop..........] ## What happens
20260527.113208.802 [<kpop..........] `pytest tests` **does start**, but it stops during **collection** with **38 errors**. Pytest is not missing and `tests/` is
20260527.113209.050 [<kpop..........] found. Every error traces to the same root:
20260527.113209.058 [<kpop..........] ```text
20260527.113209.351 [<kpop..........] ImportError: .../src/enn/enn_rust.cpython-312-x86_64-linux-gnu.so: undefined symbol: cblas_dgemm
20260527.113209.482 [<kpop..........] ImportError: Rust extension submodule `enn.enn_rust` is not available
20260527.113209.514 [<kpop..........] ```
20260527.113209.944 [<kpop..........] So no tests run: anything that imports `enn` (directly or via lazy imports) fails before the first assertion.
20260527.113210.513 [<kpop..........] **Claim (with evidence):** Collection fails because `enn_rust.so` cannot load, not because pytest or the `tests` path is
20260527.113211.154 [<kpop..........] wrong. Evidence: pytest 8.3.4, `collected 387 items / 38 errors`, traceback through `src/enn/_rust.py`.
20260527.113211.220 [<kpop..........] ## Root cause
20260527.113211.653 [<kpop..........] The editable extension at `src/enn/enn_rust.cpython-312-x86_64-linux-gnu.so` (built today ~11:27) was linked against
20260527.113212.443 [<kpop..........] **`libblas.so.3`** and **`liblapack.so.3`**, but the code also needs **CBLAS** symbols (`cblas_dgemm`, `cblas_ddot`).
20260527.113212.461 [<kpop..........] In your `yubo` conda env:
20260527.113212.898 [<kpop..........] - `libblas.so.3` — **does not** export `cblas_dgemm`
20260527.113213.224 [<kpop..........] - `libcblas.so.3` / `libopenblas.so.0` — **do** export it
20260527.113213.782 [<kpop..........] The `.so` lists `libblas.so.3` in `DT_NEEDED` but not `libcblas`, so the dynamic loader never resolves those symbols →
20260527.113213.878 [<kpop..........] import fails → pytest collection fails.
20260527.113214.482 [<kpop..........] This matches the repo’s intent in `rust/crates/ennbo/src/link_search.rs`: when `CONDA_PREFIX` is set, the build should
20260527.113215.062 [<kpop..........] prefer **`libopenblas.so`** (which includes CBLAS). This binary ended up on split reference BLAS instead.
20260527.113215.169 [<kpop..........] ## What is *not* the problem
20260527.113215.675 [<kpop..........] - **Not** “pytest can’t find tests” — it finds 387 items.
20260527.113216.448 [<kpop..........] - **Not** PYTHONPATH for py3.12 — `pyproject.toml` sets `pythonpath = ["src", "."]`, and `enn` is found; the `.so` load
20260527.113216.497 [<kpop..........] fails.
20260527.113216.907 [<kpop..........] - **Not** a duplicate py3.12 wheel — there is no `enn` under `lib/python3.12/site-packages`; only
20260527.113216.974 [<kpop..........] `src/enn/enn_rust...cp312...so` is used.
20260527.113217.174 [<kpop..........] ## How to verify locally (no repo edits)
20260527.113217.272 [<kpop..........] **Workaround (confirmed):**
20260527.113217.300 [<kpop..........] ```bash
20260527.113217.564 [<kpop..........] LD_PRELOAD="$CONDA_PREFIX/lib/libcblas.so.3" pytest tests
20260527.113217.601 [<kpop..........] ```
20260527.113218.195 [<kpop..........] That makes `from enn import enn_rust` succeed; a sample file (`tests/test_hypervolume.py`) passes with preload.
20260527.113218.674 [<kpop..........] **Proper fix (outside DCC):** Rebuild the extension so it links OpenBLAS (or `libcblas`) directly, e.g. `maturin develop`
20260527.113219.085 [<kpop..........] with `CONDA_PREFIX` set and a clean rebuild, so `DT_NEEDED` includes a library that exports CBLAS.
20260527.113219.103 [<kpop..........] ---
